#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Theodore's Geometry, Sequencing & Logic Week — Week Series
Age ~5 (Kindergarten) | Mathematics | Layout: journal

Causal arc: Name plane figures by their parts -> describe those figures precisely (sides,
corners) -> recognize and extend repeating patterns -> apply reflection/orientation to both
shapes and letters (the Wednesday mirror-message payoff) -> put multi-step events in order ->
sort by an attribute -> capstone Friday blends every skill into one "Grand Parade" review.

Every activity is dressed in a widened "things that go" theme (trucks, trains, planes, boats),
one vehicle per day, building to a Friday parade that mixes them all.

Narrator: Ziggy the Helicopter, who flies to visit a different real vehicle every day and always
looks *down* at it first -- a helicopter's-eye view is a natural excuse to notice shapes, what
comes next, and how things look from a different angle (which pays off hard on Wednesday).

New HTML renderer kinds added for this week (src/worksheet_html_renderer.py), reusable by future
weeks the same way barGraph/pictograph were added for the data week:
  - shapeIdWorksheet ("gallery" | "attributes" | "sort" | "pattern" | "mirror_match" modes) --
    real CSS/SVG-drawn plane figures, not emoji.
  - pictureSequenceWorksheet -- shuffled step cards with a number-box for ordering.
  - mirrorMessageWorksheet ("intro" | "trace" modes) -- the whole letter ROW is mirrored via a
    single CSS transform: scaleX(-1), so both letter order and letter shape flip together. What
    Theodore sees on the page is backwards; holding a real mirror to the page undoes both flips
    at once and reveals the phrase in order, right-side up.

Standards (Virginia SOL, Math, Grade K):
  Monday    -- VA.MATH.K.k.10 (identify/describe/compare plane figures), VA.MATH.K.k.12 (sort by
               one attribute)
  Tuesday   -- VA.MATH.K.k.10 (describe plane figures), VA.MATH.K.k.13 (identify, describe,
               extend, create, transfer repeating patterns)
  Wednesday -- VA.MATH.K.k.10c (identify plane figures regardless of position/orientation in
               space -- the standards-book description of exactly what a mirror does)
  Thursday  -- VA.MATH.K.k.12 (sort by one attribute: water vs. land), VA.MATH.K.k.2b (compare
               and order sets from least to greatest)
  Friday    -- capstone review of K.k.10, K.k.12, K.k.13, K.k.2

Bonus backup activities: 4 real vehicle-brand logos/emblems, converted to coloring-page line art
(PIL grayscale + CONTOUR filter) and embedded as base64 data URIs so this script fully reproduces
the week offline with no network dependency. Personal, non-commercial, non-distributed home use.
Sources (Wikimedia Commons, licence-checked at fetch time):
  - Mack Trucks badge photo -- CC BY-SA 4.0, "Mack Truck Logo.jpg"
  - Union Pacific Railroad shield -- Public domain, "Union pacific railroad logo.svg"
  - NASA insignia (2003-2015 colours) -- Public domain (U.S. federal government work)
  - U.S. Coast Guard Academy seal -- Public domain, "Us coast guard logo.png"

Output: theodore_geometry_week_series/theodore_geometry_week.html
        theodore_geometry_week_series/theodore_geometry_week_teacher_guide.html
"""

